                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Introduction"><p>The School of Gender and Development Studies (SOGDS), established in 2007, aims at achieving gender justice and equity through developing and launching academic programmes in the areas of Gender and Development studies as well as Women’s and Gender studies. Through its academic programmes, the School promotes conceptual, analytical and critical understanding of gender issues in an effort to bring about affirmative social transformations. The School examines the existing gender gap and addresses the issue of gender disparity, with the objectives of strengthening individual and institutional efforts to bring about gender equity and social justice.</p></div>

                                        
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Aboutus"  ><p>The School of Gender and Development Studies engages with:<ul>
<li>Designing and developing academic programmes and courses at research, post graduate, undergraduate and awareness levels;</li>
<li>Conducting research and developing appropriate research methodology; and</li>
<li>Formulating and implementing training programmes.</li></ul></p>
 
<p>Programmes are currently offered under two broad streams: Gender and Development Studies and Women’s and Gender Studies. Other focal areas within these broad streams include Literature, Culture, Law, Science and Agriculture among others.</p>
</div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-3" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Objectives"  ><p>The School envisions itself to have been constituted for attainment of a fair and equal society by focusing on knowledge creation, knowledge dissemination, critical thinking, research, training, sensitization and advocacy. Towards this end, the School wishes to pursue relevant courses and various other intellectual activities. The School envisions its future with great expectations and is committed to working towards the attainment of an equitable society where all gender segments get full opportunity to realize their aspirations of self-development.</p>
<p>The School envisages major initiatives in research, teaching, training and advocacy in the areas of Women's and Gender Studies as well as gender and development studies.</p></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-4" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p>Welcome to School of Gender and Development Studies (SOGDS)!  The School is a unique initiative of Indira Gandhi National Open University – the only full-fledged School in the country devoted to creating change agents ushering in gender equality and gender equity in society. We are happy to share with you details about our vision for the School and its activities. The academic programmes we offer are benefiting both national and international target audiences. From undergraduate and postgraduate degree, diploma and certificate programmes to research programmes, the School offers a rich, diverse and wide range of academic programmes designed and developed with inputs from leading experts across the country. Our programmes encourage learners to acquire and upgrade their qualifications and competencies equipping them to meet personal and professional goals.</p>
<p>The job opportunities that await our learners span governmental and non-governmental as well as corporate sectors; media organizations; international organizations such as the UN, multilateral and bilateral agencies; and specialized training institutions among others.</p>
<p>We continue to engage with our most valued learners, experts, academic contributors and counsellors. We look forward to your suggestions and feedback which will provide encouragement and impetus to our future efforts.</p>
<br>
<p style="text-align: right">
Prof. Annu J. Thomas<br>
Director,<br>
School of Gender and Development Studies</p></div>
